# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Tooling / repo anidado de la wiki (repo aparte)
.atl/
Docs/vivi-perfilamiento-leads.wiki/

# Binarios compilados
bin/

# Compiled SPA output is versioned: //go:embed packages the exact tree
# reviewed in Git. Regenerate it with `npm run heroku-postbuild` when web/
# changes; the Node lifecycle verifies every index.html asset before Go builds.

# Node
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# Local non-repository folder and files
archivos_locales/
*.rar
*.zip

# Excel source data (privacy — solo se commitea el JSON generado)
data/*.xlsx
data/*.html
data/*_files/
data/informacion_desglozada_proyectos/

# Local Heroku diagnostic screenshots (may contain sensitive configuration)
Pruebas-Heroku/
